ation-induced cell death in human T lymphocytes</article-title><source>J Exp Med</source><year>1995</year><volume>181</volume><fpage>71</fpage><lpage>77</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7528780</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><label>19</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Chinnaiyan</surname><given-names>AM</given-names></name><name><surname>O'Rourke</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Yu</surname><given-names>G-L</given-names></name><name><surname>Lyons</surname><given-names>RH</given-names></name><name><surname>Garg</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Duan</surname><given-names>DR</given-names></name><name><surname>Xing</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Gentz</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Ni</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Dixit</surname><given-names>VM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Signal transduction by DR3, a death domain&#x02013;containing receptor related to TNFR-1 and CD95</article-title><source>Science (Wash  DC)</source><year>1996</year><volume>274</volume><fpage>990</fpage><lpage>992</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8875942</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><label>20</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Brojatsch</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Naughton</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Rolls</surname><given-names>MM</given-names></name><name><surname>Zingler</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Young</surname><given-names>JAT</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>CAR1, a TNFR-related protein, is a cellular receptor for cytopathic avian leukosis-sarcoma viruses and mediates apoptosis</article-title><source>Cell</source><year>1996</year><volume>87</volume><fpage>845</fpage><lpage>855</lpage><pub-